[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     57[0m:[38;5;10m[49m In `main`, `luggage_id`, `flight_id`, `departure` and `arrival` are declared
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     58[0m:[38;5;10m[49m inside the `while (1)` loop and never initialised (only `comments[0]` is
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     59[0m:[38;5;10m[49m zeroed). A `%[...]` conversion that fails leaves its buffer untouched, but the
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     60[0m:[38;5;10m[49m record is appended anyway, so `strcpy` copies whatever was in the buffer. On
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     61[0m:[38;5;10m[49m the second and later iterations that is the previous record's value — the Rust
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     62[0m:[38;5;10m[49m code already reproduced this by hoisting the buffers out of the loop. On the
