[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     79[0m:[38;5;10m[49m **Caveat.** This is undefined behaviour in the C program. The value is a
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     80[0m:[38;5;10m[49m property of the compiler, the C library and the dynamic loader, not of the
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     81[0m:[38;5;10m[49m source, and a different toolchain will leave a different byte there — an `-O2`
